"""Deli Counter 0.235.0: a wall may not stand under a hole in its ceiling (layout_lint L27); the open-floor table
slides a hole off a wall it stands (roadmap 260).

Found by cold run 9338 (restaurant_row_001, deli_a03, the first run on 0.234.0): the table's kitchen wall at x 7 stood
under the delis' 2.2 m drop at (8, -4), its centreline 0.1 m inside the hole's edge and its new door under the hole;
frames of it in docs/cold_runs/cold_9338/, measured across the library in docs/findings/open_floor_table_260/
(holes_over_walls.py, then L27 itself: the six delis and nothing else the table made).

What it changes (anchored; each file pinned by hash; nothing written on a miss; every file LF):
  * layout_lint.py -- L27: ceiling_holes, ceiling_hole_walls, ceiling_hole_findings; lint_spec asks it (WARN).
  * open_floor_rules.py -- _clear_holes; _close slides a hole off a wall it lays; apply refuses a pair that would stand
    a wall under a hole it could not slide, and slides one off a WALL pair's wall already standing.
  * migrate_open_floor_rules.py -- its docstring says what running it again does.
  * test_ceiling_holes.py (new, 9).
  * VERSION 0.234.0 -> 0.235.0, CHANGELOG.

AFTER APPLYING, in deli_counter/: migrate_open_floor_rules.py (the six delis), migrate_furnish_recipes.py (three
move), catalog.py, the suite, build.py --all (open_floor_rules.py is a geometry source), check.py.

    python patches/patch_dc_ceiling_holes.py
"""
